# Run Local Flask Application

The goal is to start the Flask application locally using Docker Compose since the user encountered issues with GitHub. We will focus on the `flask-dev` service which includes hot-reloading and debug mode.

## Proposed Changes

No code changes are required. We will execute the following commands to start the local environment.

### Docker Compose
- Run `docker compose up -d flask-dev` to start the development container.
- This will map host port 5007 to container port 5000.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Check container status: `docker ps --filter name=flask-dev`
- Check logs: `docker logs flask-dev`

### Manual Verification
- Access the application at `http://localhost:5007` in the browser.
- Verify the index page loads correctly.
